      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Competitive binding was used to determine the number of binding sites to glucocorticoid hormones in peripheral blood leukocytes of normal subjects, patients with unstable angina pectoris and patients with myocardial infarction. A sharp (2-3-fold) increase in the number of binding sites was observed in patients with myocardial infarction during the first 24 hours after the onset of the disease."},
